Semiconductor wafer bonding equipment comprises high precision tools that join two or more wafers using direct, adhesive, metal, or anodic bonding techniques. These systems create multi layer structures essential for 3D integrated circuits, MEMS sensors, photonic modules, and heterogeneous integration across a broad spectrum of applications, from smartphones to autonomous vehicle processors.
What is Semiconductor Wafer Bonding Equipment?
Semiconductor wafer bonding equipment enables the physical and electrical integration of stacked silicon wafers. By applying controlled temperature, pressure, and alignment, the equipment forms reliable interconnects that support ultra dense routing, low loss signal transmission, and superior thermal management. The technology underpins key processes such as direct wafer bonding, hybrid copper to copper bonding, and glass frit anodic bonding, each tailored to specific performance and cost targets.
